# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# aiSlang local state
.aislang/

# Local skill caches (each dev's own running deltas — see
# .claude/skills/code-stat/SKILL.md + perf-stat/SKILL.md).
# Committed skill files are tracked; their state files are not.
.claude/skills/*/cache.*

# `aislang apply` writes stack.yml into the source dir; it embeds
# absolute host paths (litellm volume mount) so it's machine-specific
# — NOT for commit. Regenerate with `aislang plan` / `aislang apply`.
stack.yml

# Secrets / env
.env
.env.*
# …but DO commit the templates (safe, all values blank).  The
# per-project `.env.example` is emitted by `aislang plan`; the
# operator-facing `.env.cloud.example` is emitted by `aislang
# cloud init` (v0.4 W23 Mon follow-up — see crates/aislang-cloud/
# src/env_template.rs).
!.env.example
!.env.cloud.example
.secrets/
*.key
*.pem

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Allow lockfile (this is a binary crate — Cargo.lock should be committed)
!Cargo.lock

# mdbook build output (docs.aislang.cloud)
docs-site/book/
